{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"deb4631b-9484-4ccc-a2e5-04634190b26a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Note CI windows-dotnet job runs build/test in windows/ and admin/ dirs only — our tests under tests/windows/win-diagnostics won't be run by current CI. But we're only allowed to modify tests/windows/win-diagnostics/. So \"面向 GitHub Actions\" means the test project is ready; the CI wiring would be another task (ci-guards owns .github/). We can note in README that CI must add a step. Fine.\n\nNow understand the test requirements more precisely:\n\nA3: \"单测：注入一个错误，断言显示的是用户可读文案且不含堆栈\". So ErrorPresenter likely has `Present(string code)` or `Present(Exception)`. Let's design to cover both possibilities in a way that is resilient and honest.\n\nCould create tests that use reflection to find:\n- A public static method `string Present(string)` → assert map.\n- If not found, search for a public static method returning string with one `Exception` param → invoke with synthetic exception containing a marker and assert output has no \"at \" and no exception type name.\n\nBut that's speculative. The task explicitly says \"被测类型名 ErrorPresenter/LogRedactor/InviteCode.IsValid 来自 brief，命名空间待对齐放顶部\". Only namespace待对齐. For methods, brief gives `InviteCode.IsValid` fully. For LogRedactor, method unknown. For ErrorPresenter, method unknown. We should define method names as constants at top (\"待写手交付后对齐\"). That's what they asked: \"需要产品入口时，在脚本顶部集中定义成常量/待定项，并注释'待写手交付后对齐'\".\n\nSo ProductSurface.cs:\n```csharp\n// 待写手交付后对齐：命名空间与入口方法名来自 brief 的占位值，不是最终事实。\ninternal static class ProductSurface\n{\n    internal const string Namespace = \"OsakaConnect.Windows.Diagnostics\";\n    internal const string ErrorPresenterType = Namespace + \".ErrorPresenter\";\n    internal const string ErrorPresenterMethod = \"Present\";\n    internal const string LogRedactorType = Namespace + \".LogRedactor\";\n    internal const string LogRedactorMethod = \"Redact\";\n    internal const string InviteCodeType = Namespace + \".InviteCode\";\n    internal const string InviteCodeIsValid = \"IsValid\";\n}\n```\n\nReflection resolver: try Type.GetType(typeName) (works for types in current assembly? no); iterate AppDomain.CurrentDomain.GetAssemblies() and GetType(fullName); if no product assembly loaded, try Assembly.Load candidates? Candidate assembly names unknown; maybe scan repo windows/ for csproj and load built dll? Not in test process. If the product project is referenced in the test csproj conditionally, the assembly will be a dependency and loaded automatically only if a type is directly used — reflection may not trigger load. `Assembly.Load(\"...\")` needed. To handle both, define assembly name constant too, and attempt `Assembly.Load(ProductAssemblyName)`. If a ProjectReference is present, this succeeds. If not, skip.\n\ncsproj conditional project reference:\n```xml\n<!-- 待写手交付后对齐：产品工程路径预计为 windows/WinDiagnostics/WinDiagnostics.csproj。 -->\n<ItemGroup Condition=\"Exists('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\\..\\..\\windows\\WinDiagnostics\\WinDiagnostics.csproj')\">\n  <ProjectReference Include=\"$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\\..\\..\\windows\\WinDiagnostics\\WinDiagnostics.csproj\" />\n</ItemGroup>\n```\nBut we don't know path. Maybe better to include a `Directory.Build.props`-free placeholder property that writer aligns. Hmm — is it acceptable that tests don't auto-link after product delivery? The task says \"写 xUnit 测试（读共享向量文件，按相对仓库根路径定位），被测类型名 ... 命名空间待对齐放顶部\". So top constants are the alignment point. Fine.\n\nBut if the product assembly isn't referenced, reflection can't load its types. We need a ProjectReference or direct compile-time usage. The cleanest: reference the product project unconditionally once known. Since unknown, use an MSBuild property `ProductProject` with a default best-guess and a comment; and also try direct source? Another approach: use `Compile` include of product source files? No, then tests compile against them, but path unknown and would break when absent.\n\nWait — conditional ProjectReference with condition on a property:\n```xml\n<PropertyGroup>\n  <!-- 待写手交付后对齐：产品工程路径 -->\n  <ProductProject Condition=\"'$(ProductProject)' == ''\">$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\\..\\..\\windows\\WinDiagnostics\\WinDiagnostics.csproj</ProductProject>\n</PropertyGroup>\n<ItemGroup Condition=\"Exists('$(ProductProject)')\">\n  <ProjectReference Include=\"$(ProductProject)\" />\n</ItemGroup>\n```\nCI could pass `-p:ProductProject=...`. Also document in README. This is robust: today missing → no ref → tests skip. Later writer/test align one property + namespace constants.\n\nHowever, xUnit v2 custom skip attribute: Let's think whether attribute constructor discovery works. In xUnit v2, `FactAttribute` instances are created via reflection from `[Fact]` metadata; the runner checks `Skip` property. Our derived attribute:\n\n```csharp\ninternal sealed class ProductFactAttribute : FactAttribute\n{\n    public ProductFactAttribute()\n    {\n        if (!ProductSurface.Available)\n            Skip = ProductSurface.SkipReason;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nBut `FactAttribute` in xUnit v3 is sealed? In v3, FactAttribute is not sealed? v3 has `FactAttribute` maybe sealed. With v2 it's not sealed (people derive). v2 it's `public class FactAttribute : Attribute`. Yes.\n\nIn v3, skip property? v3's FactAttribute has `Skip` with init? Not sure. Stick to v2.\n\nxUnit v2 dynamic skip isn't needed. Custom attribute sets Skip at discovery. Also `[Theory]` variants `InlineData` needs `TheoryAttribute` derived similarly. We can avoid theories and use Fact with loops. Simpler: each Fact covers all vectors with loop. Use custom ProductFact on each.\n\nNow the \"待测：模块未交付\" output: skip reason string = \"待测：模块未交付\". xUnit console shows skipped with reason. Good.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: Is the \"product delivered\" detection based on type existence at attribute construction? At discovery, the test assembly is loaded. Product assembly if ProjectReference'd will be loadable. Fine.\n\nBetter: keep tests structured and also print. But skipped tests' body never runs, no console output besides runner's. That's fine, the skip reason is clear.\n\nNow test content:\n\n1. ErrorPresenterTests (A3):\n   - Load shared/errors.json; for each code: expected zh. Invoke presenter(code) → assert equals expected. Assert no \"at \" and no exception type names in result. Hmm \"at \" could legitimately appear? Chinese text has no \"at \". Also assert no \"\\n\" maybe not needed. Exception type names: check for \"Exception\", \"System.\", \"StackTrace\". But \"发生内部错误\" contains no. Add a test with injected exception: how? A3 says inject an error. We can test by creating an exception-like input? Let's design ErrorPresenter call accepting the error code only. To satisfy \"注入一个错误，断言...不含堆栈\", the test can pass an error code and additionally verify the presenter's output for a known code is the shared zh text and contains neither \" at \" stack frames nor any exception CLR type names. But that's not \"injecting an exception\".\n\nPerhaps the intended product API is `ErrorPresenter.Present(Exception ex)` or `Present(string code, Exception ex)`. We can support both: reflection helper invokes method with signature:\n- If method has 1 param of type string → pass code.\n- If 1 param assignable from Exception → pass new Exception with message containing stack-ish marker.\n- If 2 params (string, Exception) → pass both.\n\nThis covers likely designs with one method name constant. But method name still unknown. Could make it flexible: find any public static method on ErrorPresenter whose parameters match `(string)` or `(Exception)` or `(string, Exception)` and returns string. That avoids inventing a name entirely. Is that too clever? It's a small function. And aligns with \"不要编造产品的函数名\" — we explicitly avoid inventing by selecting by shape. But then if product has multiple methods, ambiguity. Keep candidate method name first; fall back to shape? Simplicity: define `ErrorPresenterMethod = \"Present\"` 待定. The user explicitly said put TBD entries at top for product entry points. So use constants; no need for fancy discovery. When writer delivers, align constants. Good.\n\nFor A3 injected exception: I'll define the test to use a synthetic exception with message containing `\"at Fake.Namespace.Type.Method()\"` and type `InvalidOperationException`. But how to feed it to presenter? Assume presenter maps code; exception not used. Hmm.\n\nMaybe ErrorPresenter has a method `Present(string errorCode, Exception? ex = null)`. Unknown.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the intended contract is simpler — ErrorPresenter takes an error code from the admin-contract error response (`errors.json` codes) and returns zh. \"注入一个错误\" in acceptance means inject an error code (not an exception object). Then assert text matches errors.json and no stack. So tests:\n- For each code in errors.json, Present(code) == zh, and not contains \" at \" / \"Exception\" / \"System.\" / \"\\n   at\".\n- Inject an unknown code → presenter should fall back to INTERNAL text (a user-readable message), never echo the code/stack. Is a fallback specified? Not in shared. Skip guessing; only test known codes.\n- To explicitly demonstrate no stack leakage, craft input containing stack text and type name? E.g., unknown code `\"System.InvalidOperationException: boom\\n at Foo.Bar()\"` — presenter should not echo it. But behavior for unknown code is unspecified. Don't assert.\n\nBetter: assert known code output exactly matches zh and contains no stack marker/exception type. That satisfies \"文案来自 errors.json 且不含堆栈 'at ' / 异常类型名\". The \"注入异常\" can be realized by constructing an `InvalidOperationException` and checking its ToString isn't in output? No.\n\nI think we can add a second test that uses a synthetic exception *passed to the presenter if the entry accepts one*, but that introduces method-shape complexity. Ponytail says minimal complete. The acceptance verification says \"单测：注入一个错误，断言显示的是用户可读文案且不含堆栈\". Injecting an error code is a reasonable reading: the admin API returns an error JSON with `code`; presenter maps code → text. Let me check openapi for error schema.\n\nLet me read openapi/admin.v1.yaml error response.","signature":"deb4631b-9484-4ccc-a2e5-04634190b26a"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":25216,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec7e012c-bf97-4a00-b1a5-b32ee1d3c38b","uuid":"0514ad43-4507-4f18-9904-19dcded55d8f","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:02:56.760Z","thinking_duration_ms":15635,"thinking_display":"updates"}
