{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"1b43bebd-e701-44ef-88cf-d702f2b4b68a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ErrorBody has code and message. ErrorPresenter likely takes code → zh message. \"注入一个错误\" = pass an error body/code. I'll test code mapping.\n\nBut acceptance explicitly says \"不含堆栈 'at ' / 异常类型名\" per the task card. So test assertion: output doesn't contain \"at \" (with a space), \"Exception\", \"System.\", \"StackTrace\", \"   at\". We'll assert for each code.\n\nCould also test that when the server's ErrorBody has a `message` (possibly containing stack), presenter uses only `code` and ignores untrusted message? Not specified. Hmm, acceptance A3: \"注入一个错误，断言显示的是用户可读文案且不含堆栈\". If ErrorPresenter takes `code`, fine.\n\nLogRedactor (A4):\n- Load redaction.json: `mask` and `cases`. Call redactor on `in`, assert equals `out`. Method name unknown: `Redact`. Constant.\n- Also assert output doesn't contain original secret? The expected out encodes that. All 8 cases.\n- Entry may be instance or static. Reflection helper: if static invoke null; if instance, create via parameterless ctor (`Activator.CreateInstance`). Make constants for class.\n\nInviteCode.IsValid (A15):\n- Load invite-code.json. valid/invalid arrays. Note `null` in invalid. Product signature `static bool IsValid(string?)`. Reflection invocation with null. For valid entries including `\" 7X2KQ9MZ \"` (trim) expect true. For invalid entries false. \n- Important: assert valid all true and invalid all false separately. Include each case detail in assertion message (index and value) so failures are diagnosable. For null show \"<null>\". Also note that JSON null maps to null. Invoke with null. If method parameter is non-nullable string, runtime still passes null fine.\n\nTest data loader:\n- Resolve repo root by walking up from AppContext.BaseDirectory until a directory containing `shared/test-vectors/redaction.json`. That's robust. Use `System.Text.Json` (built-in) to parse. No extra deps.\n- For errors.json: `Dictionary<string, ErrorInfo>` with `http` and `zh`.\n\nReflection helpers:\n```csharp\ninternal static class ProductSurface\n{\n    internal static bool TryGetType(string fullName, out Type type) { ... }\n    internal static object? InvokeStatic(Type type, string methodName, params object?[] args)\n    internal static object? Invoke(Type type, string methodName, params object?[] args) // static or instance\n}\n```\nNeed to load product assembly. `Type.GetType(fullName)` searches mscorlib and calling assembly only. Scan `AppDomain.CurrentDomain.GetAssemblies()`. If product assembly not loaded, try `Assembly.Load(new AssemblyName(ProductAssemblyName))` (constant TBD). If all fail, skip.\n\nCustom attribute:\n```csharp\ninternal sealed class ProductFactAttribute : FactAttribute\n{\n    public ProductFactAttribute()\n    {\n        if (!ProductSurface.IsAvailable)\n            Skip = ProductSurface.NotDelivered;\n    }\n}\n```\nBut ProductSurface.IsAvailable needs to resolve all three types? Each test class needs only its own type. Attribute can take a product type name? Since attributes require compile-time constant args: `[ProductFact(ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterType)]`. But ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterType is a const string, OK. Then constructor checks that one type. However, the types are all in the same namespace; if one exists, all likely. Simpler: `IsAvailable` checks namespace/assembly. But if the type resolution uses method names at test runtime, fine.\n\nDesign:\n```csharp\ninternal sealed class ProductFactAttribute : FactAttribute\n{\n    public ProductFactAttribute(string typeName)\n    {\n        if (!ProductSurface.CanResolve(typeName))\n            Skip = ProductSurface.NotDelivered;\n    }\n}\n```\nUsage: `[ProductFact(ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterType)]`.\n\nBut attributes run at discovery; if product is delivered but method name differs, test runs and fails — that's correct (alignment issue).\n\nReflection invocation:\n```csharp\ninternal static object? Call(Type type, string methodName, params object?[] args)\n{\n    var flags = BindingFlags.Public | BindingFlags.Static | BindingFlags.Instance;\n    var method = type.GetMethods(flags).Single(m => m.Name == methodName && m.GetParameters().Length == args.Length);\n    var target = method.IsStatic ? null : Activator.CreateInstance(type);\n    return method.Invoke(target, args);\n}\n```\nIf type has ctor args, fails. Fine, align later.\n\nFor LogRedactor maybe method is `Redact(string)`. For ErrorPresenter maybe `Present(string)`. For InviteCode static `IsValid`.\n\n\"只准改 tests/windows/win-diagnostics/ 下的文件\" — create directory and files.\n\nFiles:\n1. `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/WinDiagnostics.Tests.csproj`\n2. `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/ProductSurface.cs` (TBD constants + reflection + ProductFact attribute)\n3. `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/SharedVectors.cs` (repo root + JSON loading + models)\n4. `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/ErrorPresenterTests.cs` (A3)\n5. `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/LogRedactorTests.cs` (A4)\n6. `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/InviteCodeTests.cs` (A15)\n7. `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/README.md` (run cmd, prerequisites, \"待 CI\", coverage, alignment points)\n\nEach script file top comments: 用途、前置环境、运行命令、覆盖的 acceptance 编号. For C# test files, add block comments at top. For csproj, XML comment. For ProductSurface / SharedVectors, comment too.\n\nNow: can I validate compile locally? Task says \"本机不装 JDK/SDK/.NET、不跑构建\". So no. I must not run dotnet. I can still review syntax carefully. Maybe use a C# syntax check tool? None available. Be careful.\n\nOne concern: xUnit v2 `FactAttribute` constructor signature and Skip property. In xUnit v2, `Xunit.FactAttribute` has `public string? Skip { get; set; }` (v2) — yes, on FactAttribute? Actually `Skip` is defined on `FactAttribute` in xunit.core: `public string? Skip { get; set; }`. Yes.\n\nPackage versions: \n- Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 17.11.1 (exists, Aug 2024)\n- xunit 2.9.2 (exists, Sep 2024)\n- xunit.runner.visualstudio 2.8.2 (exists, May 2024; requires xunit >= 2.9? compatible)\nPrivateAssets all.\n\nTargetFramework net8.0. IsWindows? Tests are pure logic, can run on Windows per CI. No WPF reference needed (product assembly might be WPF; referencing net8.0-windows WPF project from net8.0 project fails!). Important: if product is a WPF app targeting `net8.0-windows` with `<UseWPF>`, a net8.0 test project cannot reference it (incompatible TFM). The test csproj should target `net8.0-windows` too. Since runtime windows-latest, use `net8.0-windows`. That can reference net8.0 libraries and net8.0-windows. Add `<UseWPF>false</UseWPF>`? Not needed. `net8.0-windows` is fine. Also could set `<EnableWindowsTargeting>true</EnableWindowsTargeting>` to allow restore on Linux, but we don't run locally; harmless and helps. Actually `net8.0-windows` builds on Linux with EnableWindowsTargeting true. Add it for flexibility. But WPF ProjectReference on Linux won't build; irrelevant. CI windows-latest.\n\nShould test project reference Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk? Yes.\n\nRepo root location: test project's output at `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/bin/Debug/net8.0-windows/`. Walk up to find `shared/test-vectors`. Good.\n\nJSON models:\n```csharp\ninternal sealed class RedactionVectors { public string Mask {get;set;} = \"\"; public List<RedactionCase> Cases {get;set;} = new(); }\ninternal sealed class RedactionCase { public string In {get;set;} = \"\"; public string Out {get;set;} = \"\"; }\n```\n`in` is a C# keyword; property name `In` maps case-insensitively? System.Text.Json default is case-sensitive exact match unless PropertyNameCaseInsensitive = true. JSON key \"in\" vs property \"In\": with default options, no match → In remains \"\". Use `[JsonPropertyName(\"in\")]` and `[JsonPropertyName(\"out\")]`. Need `using System.Text.Json.Serialization;`.\n\nInviteCode vectors: `{\"valid\":[...], \"invalid\":[...]}` with null. Model `List<string?>`.\n\nErrors: `Dictionary<string, ErrorEntry>`; ErrorEntry { int Http; string Zh } with options `PropertyNameCaseInsensitive = true` (keys \"http\",\"zh\" match `Http`/`Zh` case-insensitively). Add.\n\nTest assertions:\nErrorPresenterTests:\n```csharp\n[ProductFact(ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterType)]\npublic void A3_EveryErrorCodeShowsSharedChineseText()\n{\n    var errors = SharedVectors.LoadErrors();\n    Assert.NotEmpty(errors);\n    var type = ProductSurface.Resolve(ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterType);\n    foreach (var (code, entry) in errors)\n    {\n        var shown = (string?)ProductSurface.Call(type, ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterMethod, code);\n        Assert.False(string.IsNullOrEmpty(shown), ...);\n        Assert.Equal(entry.Zh, shown);\n        AssertNoStack(shown, code);\n    }\n}\n\n[ProductFact(...)]\npublic void A3_NoStackOrExceptionTypeInPresentedText()\n{\n   // 注入一个带堆栈形状的异常，传给 Presenter 可接受的入口? \n}\n```\nHmm second test. Let me implement an \"injected error\" test that constructs a fake error code? Actually we can formulate: The presenter output for a real error code must not contain any substring from the injected exception's `ToString()`, and not stack markers. Inject an `InvalidOperationException(\"injected-secret at Fake.Type.Method()\")` in the test; assert `presented` doesn't contain \"injected-secret\", \"at \", \"Fake.Type.Method\", \"InvalidOperationException\", \"System.\". But the exception isn't passed to the presenter, so this is contrived. Not honest.\n\nAlternative: define an optional presenter overload constant, and if the product method has a second Exception param, use it. Too speculative.\n\nMaybe the presenter API is likely `Present(string code, Exception? ex = null)`? No idea. Let's use method shape resolution to support both and make the exception-injection test real:\n- Find method by name `Present` (constant).\n- Inspect parameters. If it has a parameter assignable from `Exception`, invoke with the injected exception (and code if there is a string param).\n- Otherwise skip that test with a clear message? xUnit v2 dynamic skip not available. But we can make it pass only if behavior verified... Not allowed to silently pass.\n\nWe can write the exception test using the same code-based entry: inject an error whose code is valid but whose companion message contains stack; if presenter only takes code, the injection reduces to code. The acceptance wording \"注入一个错误\" doesn't necessarily mean exception object. I'll treat \"inject an error code from the shared error contract\" as the injection. To strengthen, the test input includes an `ErrorBody`-like message with stack? Product API unknown. Hmm.\n\nMaybe ErrorPresenter's entry takes the JSON error body string? Unlikely.\n\nLet me settle on two tests:\n1. `A3_KnownErrorCodeMapsToSharedChineseText_NoStackTrace` — for each errors.json entry invoke `Present(code)`, assert exact zh, and assert absence of stack markers / exception type names. This covers both A3 clauses.\n2. `A3_UntrustedMessageWithStackTraceIsNeverEchoed` — invoke presenter with an arbitrary server error code? Behavior unspecified. Skip.\n\nInstead second test: `A3_AllCodesProduceUserReadableText` duplicates. Ponytail minimal: one test with a loop and assertions suffices. But \"注入异常\" explicit: maybe add a test that constructs `Exception` and asserts `ex.ToString()` marker strings are not in presenter output for `INTERNAL`. Still contrived but documents intent. I can write:\n\n```csharp\n[ProductFact(...)]\npublic void A3_ExceptionDetailIsNotShown()\n{\n    // 注入：构造一个带类型名与堆栈帧的异常样例（模拟底层异常信息）\n    var injected = new InvalidOperationException(\"secret at Osaka.Internal.Impl.Run()\");\n    var shown = (string?)ProductSurface.Call(type, Present, \"INTERNAL\");\n    Assert.DoesNotContain(\"at \", shown); // stack marker\n    Assert.DoesNotContain(\"Exception\", shown);\n    Assert.DoesNotContain(\"Osaka.Internal\", shown); // not from injected? \n}\n```\nBut injected never reaches presenter; asserting output doesn't contain it is trivially true. That's fake-ish. Better not.\n\nCould the presenter entry be `Present(Exception ex)`? If I choose to test exception injection, I'd have to guess. The task says methods TBD. Maybe design ProductSurface with two entry constants:\n- `ErrorPresenterByCodeMethod = \"PresentCode\"` \n- `ErrorPresenterByExceptionMethod = \"PresentException\"`\nToo much.\n\nGiven the brief summary \"ErrorPresenter（errors.json 码→中文文案，不含堆栈）\", the code mapping is the function. \"不符堆栈\" means the presenter must not append exception details. I'll write one test iterating all codes with exact-match + stack assertions. The \"inject an error\" is represented by invoking each contract error code. Maybe add comment: \"注入 = 传入 shared/errors.json 中的错误码（A3 的“错误”）\". Honest and traceable.\n\nNow LogRedactor: method name `Redact` constant. Cases from vectors. Assert exact out. Also assert for cases with masked output, the secret fragment from input isn't present? Exact equality covers.\n\nInviteCode: static IsValid. Valid cases include whitespace-padded. Invalid includes null. Invoke via reflection with null. Assert bool.\n\nReflection details:\n\n```csharp\ninternal static Type Resolve(string fullTypeName)\n{\n    var type = Type.GetType(fullTypeName, throwOnError: false);\n    if (type != null) return type;\n    foreach (var asm in AppDomain.CurrentDomain.GetAssemblies())\n    {\n        type = asm.GetType(fullTypeName, throwOnError: false);\n        if (type != null) return type;\n    }\n    try\n    {\n        type = Assembly.Load(new AssemblyName(ProductAssembly)).GetType(fullTypeName, throwOnError: false);\n    }\n    catch (Exception) { }\n    if (type == null) throw new InvalidOperationException(NotDelivered + \"（找不到类型 \" + fullTypeName + \"；请对齐 ProductSurface 常量）\");\n    return type;\n}\n\ninternal static object? Call(Type type, string methodName, params object?[] args)\n{\n    var method = type.GetMethods(BindingFlags.Public | BindingFlags.Static | BindingFlags.Instance)\n        .SingleOrDefault(m => m.Name == methodName && m.GetParameters().Length == args.Length)\n        ?? throw new InvalidOperationException($\"找不到入口 {type.FullName}.{methodName}/{args.Length}；请对齐 ProductSurface 常量。\");\n    var target = method.IsStatic ? null : Activator.CreateInstance(type);\n    return method.Invoke(target, args);\n}\n```\nCould be multiple overloads same arg count → SingleOrDefault throws. Better FirstOrDefault with exact param type match? Minimal: FirstOrDefault. Use:\n```csharp\nvar method = type.GetMethods(...).FirstOrDefault(m => m.Name == methodName && m.GetParameters().Length == args.Length);\n```\nFine.\n\nAvailability:\n```csharp\ninternal static bool CanResolve(string fullTypeName)\n{\n    try { Resolve(fullTypeName); return true; } catch { return false; }\n}\n```\nBut Resolve tries Assembly.Load each time, costly but negligible. Note attribute constructor at discovery calls Resolve; if product assembly reference exists, fine.\n\nHowever: if no product project reference, `Assembly.Load(\"OsakaConnect.Windows\")` may throw FileNotFoundException; caught. Good.\n\nPotential issue: ProductSurface's `NotDelivered` constant \"待测：模块未交付\". Skip reason. Good.\n\nNaming product assembly: `OsakaConnect.Windows` TBD. But if no ProjectReference, this doesn't matter. Document.\n\nNow csproj conditional ProjectReference: Include a property + condition:\n```xml\n<PropertyGroup>\n  <!-- 待写手交付后对齐：产品工程路径；缺失时测试自动跳过并提示“待测：模块未交付”。 -->\n  <ProductProject Condition=\"'$(ProductProject)' == ''\">$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\\..\\..\\windows\\OsakaConnect.Windows\\OsakaConnect.Windows.csproj</ProductProject>\n</PropertyGroup>\n<ItemGroup Condition=\"Exists('$(ProductProject)')\">\n  <ProjectReference Include=\"$(ProductProject)\" />\n</ItemGroup>\n```\nHmm `Exists()` with relative path containing `..\\` works. But guessing path may be wrong. Better not include a guessed reference; instead document that writer/test aligns. But then when product delivered, tests skip forever unless someone adds reference — which is exactly the \"对齐\" step. Include the conditional reference with a clearly marked placeholder? The task says namespace pending, not path. I'd include the conditional with a common path but mark 待对齐. It's harmless if wrong (Exists false). It helps if right.\n\nActually there is risk: if path exists but assembly name differs, test runs and fails with \"找不到入口\". That's correct signal.\n\nCould make ProductProject overridable in CI: `dotnet test -p:ProductProject=...`.\n\nNow xUnit `Assert.DoesNotContain` overload: `Assert.DoesNotContain(string expectedSubstring, string actualString)` exists in xUnit 2. Yes. `Assert.Contains(string, string)` yes.\n\nString comparison: xUnit `Assert.Equal(expected, actual)` for strings default ordinal. Good.\n\nData loading:\n```csharp\ninternal static string RepoRoot { get; } = FindRepoRoot();\nprivate static string FindRepoRoot()\n{\n    var dir = new DirectoryInfo(AppContext.BaseDirectory);\n    while (dir != null)\n    {\n        if (Directory.Exists(Path.Combine(dir.FullName, \"shared\", \"test-vectors\")))\n            return dir.FullName;\n        dir = dir.Parent;\n    }\n    throw new InvalidOperationException(\"找不到仓库根（shared/test-vectors 不存在）\");\n}\n```\nWhere to store? Compute lazily each call to avoid static init exceptions at discovery? Attribute constructor only resolves types, not vectors. Fine. But make property method.\n\nLoad:\n```csharp\ninternal static Dictionary<string, ErrorEntry> LoadErrors() =>\n    JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, ErrorEntry>>(File.ReadAllText(Path.Combine(RepoRoot(), \"shared\", \"errors.json\")), Options)!;\n```\nOptions: `new JsonSerializerOptions { PropertyNameCaseInsensitive = true }` static readonly.\n\nRedaction model uses JsonPropertyName.\n\nAlso verify mask value matches? Not needed; use `out` expected. But could assert that every masked output contains `mask`. Not necessary.\n\nNow file header comments. Example:\n\n```csharp\n// 用途：A3 统一错误展示单测——errors.json 中每个错误码必须显示共享中文文案，且不含堆栈/异常类型名。\n// 前置环境：Windows + .NET 8 SDK；产品工程 win-diagnostics 已交付并与 ProductSurface.cs 顶部常量对齐。\n// 运行命令：dotnet test tests/windows/win-diagnostics -c Release\n// 覆盖：A3\n// 待 CI：本机不装 .NET，未在本机运行；由 GitHub Actions windows-latest 执行。\n```\n\nEach test file.\n\nREADME with run commands, prerequisites, \"待 CI\", skip behavior, alignment table, what CI wiring is needed (ci-guards adds step; we can't edit .github).\n\nCould also add `.gitignore`? .gitignore global already ignores bin/obj? Check root .gitignore content.","signature":"1b43bebd-e701-44ef-88cf-d702f2b4b68a"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":916,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":30464,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec7e012c-bf97-4a00-b1a5-b32ee1d3c38b","uuid":"dd734699-f3a2-41c6-9c9e-c86b6d548eb9","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:03:23.720Z","thinking_duration_ms":25720,"thinking_display":"updates"}
