{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"8b41fd0d-b63e-446e-b1ab-4f1e64900082","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Existing style: tests/server/server-core. Our location tests/windows/win-diagnostics. Good.\n\nCheck scope script to ensure allowed path. Task says only tests/windows/win-diagnostics/. board scope includes tests/. fine.\n\nNow write files. Let me carefully craft C#.\n\nOne thing: `ProductSurface.Call` invoking static method with null arg — `method.Invoke(null, new object?[] { null })` works. For reflection, `params object?[] args`.\n\nFor `InviteCode.IsValid`, the parameter may be `string?`; passing null is fine.\n\nFor valid/invalid vectors, JSON deserialization:\n```csharp\ninternal sealed class InviteCodeVectors\n{\n    [JsonPropertyName(\"valid\")] public List<string?> Valid { get; set; } = new();\n    [JsonPropertyName(\"invalid\")] public List<string?> Invalid { get; set; } = new();\n}\n```\n\nRedaction:\n```csharp\ninternal sealed class RedactionVectors\n{\n    [JsonPropertyName(\"mask\")] public string Mask { get; set; } = \"\";\n    [JsonPropertyName(\"cases\")] public List<RedactionCase> Cases { get; set; } = new();\n}\ninternal sealed class RedactionCase\n{\n    [JsonPropertyName(\"in\")] public string In { get; set; } = \"\";\n    [JsonPropertyName(\"out\")] public string Out { get; set; } = \"\";\n}\n```\n\nErrors:\n```csharp\ninternal sealed class ErrorEntry\n{\n    public int Http { get; set; }\n    public string Zh { get; set; } = \"\";\n}\n```\nOptions case-insensitive.\n\n`SharedVectors`:\n```csharp\nusing System.Text.Json;\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization; // not needed here if models in same file\n\ninternal static class SharedVectors\n{\n    private static readonly JsonSerializerOptions Json = new() { PropertyNameCaseInsensitive = true };\n\n    internal static string RepoRoot()\n    {\n        for (var dir = new DirectoryInfo(AppContext.BaseDirectory); dir != null; dir = dir.Parent)\n            if (Directory.Exists(Path.Combine(dir.FullName, \"shared\", \"test-vectors\")))\n                return dir.FullName;\n        throw new InvalidOperationException(\"找不到仓库根（shared/test-vectors 不存在）\");\n    }\n\n    private static string VectorPath(string name) => Path.Combine(RepoRoot(), \"shared\", \"test-vectors\", name);\n\n    internal static Dictionary<string, ErrorEntry> LoadErrors() =>\n        JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, ErrorEntry>>(\n            File.ReadAllText(Path.Combine(RepoRoot(), \"shared\", \"errors.json\")), Json)\n        ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\"shared/errors.json 解析为空\");\n\n    internal static RedactionVectors LoadRedaction() => ...;\n    internal static InviteCodeVectors LoadInviteCodes() => ...;\n}\n```\nWait: `Path.Combine(RepoRoot(), \"shared\", \"errors.json\")` - fine.\n\nStatic class containing nested model types? Put models in same file as top-level internal classes. That's fine.\n\nProductSurface:\n```csharp\nusing System.Reflection;\nusing Xunit;\n\n// 待写手交付后对齐：命名空间、程序集名与入口方法名均为 brief 占位值，不是最终事实。\ninternal static class ProductSurface\n{\n    internal const string ProductAssembly = \"OsakaConnect.Windows\";\n    internal const string Namespace = \"OsakaConnect.Windows.Diagnostics\";\n\n    internal const string ErrorPresenterType = Namespace + \".ErrorPresenter\";\n    internal const string ErrorPresenterMethod = \"Present\";   // 待写手交付后对齐：错误码→中文文案\n    internal const string LogRedactorType = Namespace + \".LogRedactor\";\n    internal const string LogRedactorMethod = \"Redact\";       // 待写手交付后对齐\n    internal const string InviteCodeType = Namespace + \".InviteCode\";\n    internal const string InviteCodeIsValidMethod = \"IsValid\";\n\n    internal const string NotDelivered = \"待测：模块未交付\";\n\n    internal static Type? TryResolve(string fullTypeName)\n    {\n        foreach (var assembly in AppDomain.CurrentDomain.GetAssemblies())\n            if (assembly.GetType(fullTypeName, throwOnError: false) is { } found)\n                return found;\n        try\n        {\n            var product = Assembly.Load(new AssemblyName(ProductAssembly));\n            return product.GetType(fullTypeName, throwOnError: false);\n        }\n        catch (Exception)\n        {\n            return null;\n        }\n    }\n\n    internal static object? Call(Type type, string methodName, params object?[] args)\n    {\n        var method = type.GetMethods(BindingFlags.Public | BindingFlags.Static | BindingFlags.Instance)\n            .FirstOrDefault(m => m.Name == methodName && m.GetParameters().Length == args.Length)\n            ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\n                $\"找不到入口 {type.FullName}.{methodName}/{args.Length}；请对齐 ProductSurface 顶部常量。\");\n        var target = method.IsStatic ? null : Activator.CreateInstance(type);\n        return method.Invoke(target, args);\n    }\n}\n\ninternal sealed class ProductFactAttribute : FactAttribute\n{\n    public ProductFactAttribute(string productType)\n    {\n        if (ProductSurface.TryResolve(productType) is null)\n            Skip = ProductSurface.NotDelivered;\n    }\n}\n```\nPotential compile issue: `is { } found` pattern with `GetType(...)` returns `Type?`; fine C# 9+. In foreach, declaration scope fine.\n\n`FactAttribute` namespace Xunit. Good. In xUnit v3 it's also Xunit but Skip maybe different; we use v2.\n\nWait: attribute classes must be public? xUnit discovers `[ProductFact]` on public test methods. If `ProductFactAttribute` is internal, attribute usage might still compile (attributes can be internal), and xUnit doesn't need to load the attribute type? The runner enumerates attributes and matches names ending with \"Fact\"? Actually xUnit v2's discoverer looks for `FactAttribute` assignable types by checking custom attributes on methods and examining `IAttributeInfo.GetNamedArgument<string>(\"Skip\")` and type assignability to `FactAttribute`. Internal is fine because it's in the test assembly. But safer make it public. Note: C# requires attribute class accessibility at least as accessible as usage; usage is on public methods in public classes; internal attribute on public method is allowed? The attribute type accessibility doesn't need to be public for usage in same assembly; compiler only checks it's accessible at use site (same assembly). Fine. But xUnit uses reflection and can instantiate internal types. Keep `public sealed class ProductFactAttribute : FactAttribute` to be safe. And ProductSurface public? Not necessary. Make ProductFactAttribute public, ProductSurface internal (const string passed from same assembly).\n\nBut `ProductFactAttribute` constructor takes `string productType` — attribute args must be constant; `ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterType` is const string. OK.\n\nTest classes public.\n\nNow test code. ErrorPresenterTests:\n\n```csharp\n// header...\nusing Xunit;\n\npublic sealed class ErrorPresenterTests\n{\n    [ProductFact(ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterType)]\n    public void A3_错误码显示共享中文文案且不含堆栈()\n    {\n        var type = ProductSurface.TryResolve(ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterType)\n            ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(...); // shouldn't happen, but nullable handling\n        var errors = SharedVectors.LoadErrors();\n        Assert.NotEmpty(errors);\n\n        foreach (var (code, entry) in errors)\n        {\n            var shown = ProductSurface.Call(type, ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterMethod, code) as string;\n\n            Assert.False(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(shown), $\"{code} 未显示可读文案\");\n            Assert.Equal(entry.Zh, shown);\n            Assert.DoesNotContain(\"at \", shown!);\n            Assert.DoesNotContain(\"Exception\", shown!);\n            Assert.DoesNotContain(\"System.\", shown!);\n            Assert.DoesNotContain(\"StackTrace\", shown!);\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\nMethod names in Chinese are valid C# identifiers? Yes, C# supports Unicode identifiers. Existing codebase uses Chinese comments but test method names in Python English. Better use English method names to avoid any tooling issues: `A3_KnownErrorCodeShowsSharedTextWithoutStackTrace`.\n\nWait: `Assert.DoesNotContain(\"at \", shown!)` — \"at \" could match in Chinese? no. Also \"Exception\" - zh doesn't have. Assert.Equal already ensures exact text; the extra checks are redundant but encode acceptance A3. Keep because acceptance explicitly requires.\n\nThe \"注入异常\" wording: Add a comment at the injection point:\n```csharp\n// 注入一个错误：取 shared/errors.json 的错误码，模拟后台返回的 ErrorBody.code。\n```\nThat's honest.\n\nBut maybe also assert the presenter ignores an injected exception-shaped message. Not possible.\n\nCould include a test `A3_NoExceptionTypeNameForInternalError` with an exception? Skip.\n\nLogRedactorTests:\n```csharp\n[ProductFact(ProductSurface.LogRedactorType)]\npublic void A4_AllRedactionVectorsMatch()\n{\n    var type = ...;\n    var vectors = SharedVectors.LoadRedaction();\n    Assert.NotEmpty(vectors.Cases);\n    for (var i = 0; i < vectors.Cases.Count; i++)\n    {\n        var c = vectors.Cases[i];\n        var redacted = ProductSurface.Call(type, ProductSurface.LogRedactorMethod, c.In) as string;\n        Assert.True(redacted is not null, $\"case #{i}\");\n        Assert.Equal(c.Out, redacted);\n    }\n}\n```\nMaybe also mask marker present for masked outputs? Exact match enough.\n\nInviteCodeTests:\n```csharp\n[ProductFact(ProductSurface.InviteCodeType)]\npublic void A15_AllInviteCodeVectors()\n{\n    var type = ...;\n    var vectors = SharedVectors.LoadInviteCodes();\n    Assert.NotEmpty(vectors.Valid);\n    Assert.NotEmpty(vectors.Invalid);\n\n    for (var i = 0; i < vectors.Valid.Count; i++)\n    {\n        var code = vectors.Valid[i];\n        Assert.True((bool)ProductSurface.Call(type, ProductSurface.InviteCodeIsValidMethod, code)!,\n            $\"合法向量 #{i} 被判非法：{Show(code)}\");\n    }\n    for (var i = 0; i < vectors.Invalid.Count; i++)\n    {\n        var code =