wn);\n            Assert.DoesNotContain(\"Exception\", shown);\n            Assert.DoesNotContain(\"System.\", shown);\n            Assert.DoesNotContain(\"StackTrace\", shown);\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\nNullable warning: `shown` is string? after `Assert.False(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(shown))` compiler doesn't know non-null; `Assert.Equal(entry.Zh, shown)` fine (nullable). `Assert.DoesNotContain(\"at \", shown)` expects non-null string; compile warning CS8604 (warnings not errors unless TreatWarningsAsErrors). Could do `var text = shown!;`. Cleaner:\n\n```csharp\nAssert.NotNull(shown);\nAssert.Equal(entry.Zh, shown);\nAssert.DoesNotContain(\"at \", shown!);\n```\n\nActually xUnit's Assert.NotNull has `[NotNull]` annotation in recent versions, so flow analysis knows. xunit.assert 2.9 includes nullable annotations with `NotNull` attribute? Yes, xUnit 2.4+ has nullable annotations. `Assert.NotNull(shown)` should refine to non-null via [NotNull]. To be safe use `shown!` everywhere after.\n\nLogRedactor:\n```csharp\npublic sealed class LogRedactorTests\n{\n    [ProductFact(ProductSurface.LogRedactorType)]\n    public void A4_AllRedactionVectorsAreMasked()\n    {\n        var type = ...;\n        var vectors = SharedVectors.LoadRedaction();\n        Assert.NotEmpty(vectors.Cases);\n\n        for (var i = 0; i < vectors.Cases.Count; i++)\n        {\n            var item = vectors.Cases[i];\n            var redacted = ProductSurface.Call(type, ProductSurface.LogRedactorMethod, item.In) as string;\n            Assert.False(redacted is null, $\"redaction 向量 #{i} 无输出\");\n            Assert.Equal(item.Out, redacted);\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nInviteCode:\n```csharp\npublic sealed class InviteCodeTests\n{\n    [ProductFact(ProductSurface.InviteCodeType)]\n    public void A15_AllInviteCodeVectorsPass()\n    {\n        var type = ...;\n        var vectors = SharedVectors.LoadInviteCodes();\n        Assert.NotEmpty(vectors.Valid);\n        Assert.NotEmpty(vectors.Invalid);\n\n        for (var i = 0; i < vectors.Valid.Count; i++)\n            AssertValid(type, vectors.Valid[i], true, $\"合法向量 #{i}\");\n        for (var i = 0; i < vectors.Invalid.Count; i++)\n            AssertValid(type, vectors.Invalid[i], false, $\"非法向量 #{i}\");\n    }\n\n    private static void AssertValid(Type type, string? code, bool expected, string label)\n    {\n        var result = ProductSurface.Call(type, ProductSurface.InviteCodeIsValidMethod, code);\n        Assert.True(result is bool actual && actual == expected, $\"{label} 判定错误：{Show(code)}，期望 IsValid={expected}\");\n    }\n\n    private static string Show(string? code) => code is null ? \"<null>\" : $\"\\\"{code}\\\"\";\n}\n```\nNote message interpolation with Chinese. Fine.\n\nHeader comments include \"待 CI\".\n\nLet me write.","signature":"fcde0a3d-3e57-4f7c-83cc-1062595e5564"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4325,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":39424,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec7e012c-bf97-4a00-b1a5-b32ee1d3c38b","uuid":"0363ff80-2857-4c3a-a4d6-c62e6fc0af73","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:04:02.840Z","thinking_duration_ms":5955,"thinking_display":"updates"}
