t's `public string? Skip { get; set; }` too? v3 FactAttribute has `Skip` property but dynamic skip uses `Assert.Skip`. Fine.\n\nPotential xUnit analyzer: xUnit1000 \"Test classes must be public\" — ours are public. xUnit1013 \"Public method should be marked as test\" — our only public methods are test methods, plus Show private. ProductFactAttribute's constructor public override? It's an attribute class, analyzer xUnit1013 applies to test classes? It might complain public constructor in non-test class? Attribute is not a test class. Fine.\n\nOne concern: xUnit analyzer xUnit1026? \"Theory methods should use all of their parameters\" - Fact no params. Fine.\n\nAnother concern: `ProductFactAttribute` ctor takes string; `[ProductFact(ProductSurface.ErrorPresenterType)]` const expression concatenated from consts — const. Good.\n\nAnother: xUnit discovery might reject custom FactAttribute if it doesn't implement `ITestMethod`? No.\n\nNow: does xUnit v2 skip at discovery based on Skip property set in ctor? The runner creates attribute instances via `Reflector.GetCustomAttributes` (which includes constructor side effects), then reads Skip. Yes. This is standard technique (e.g., conditional fact attributes set Skip in ctor). Good.\n\nNow check scope script won't complain about files: board scope includes \"tests/\". Also protected only .codex/.claude. Fine.\n\nLet me run scripts/check-scope.sh? It requires base ref perhaps. Could run with main to verify paths. It's read-only. Let's inspect script first.","signature":"c5b2f9d2-08ac-4acf-b8a7-5fe4ff157f1a"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":243,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":47232,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec7e012c-bf97-4a00-b1a5-b32ee1d3c38b","uuid":"55fe8915-7b67-486f-a430-6849cfab4f4a","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:04:20.370Z","thinking_duration_ms":5447,"thinking_display":"updates"}
