{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"1e5a9ac3-d8ce-49ea-9aea-ec343842ed8b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Scope check needs approval; skip it — the analysis shows paths are in global scope. But wait, git status shows `tests/android/` untracked too (another session's work in this shared worktree?). Not ours. And result logs. We shouldn't touch.\n\nInteresting: `tests/android/` exists now (created by another session concurrently). Not our concern.\n\nNow, can I verify C# syntax without .NET? Perhaps `csc`/mono not installed. Task says don't run build, so no.\n\nLet me do a careful read-through of files for errors.\n\nPotential issue in SharedVectors: `using System.Text.Json.Serialization;` for JsonPropertyName. Yes.\n\nPotential issue: `JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, ErrorEntry>>(string, options)` exists. Yes.\n\nPotential issue: `File.ReadAllText(Path.Combine(RepoRoot(), \"shared\", \"test-vectors\", \"redaction.json\"))` fine.\n\nPotential issue: `DirectoryInfo`/`AppContext.BaseDirectory` — output dir is `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/bin/Release/net8.0-windows/`. Walking up: net8.0-windows → Release → bin → win-diagnostics → windows → tests → repo root (contains shared). Yes.\n\nPotential issue: test project default `ProductProject` computed as `$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\\..\\..\\windows\\...`. From `tests/windows/win-diagnostics/`, `..\\..\\..` = repo root? Let's count: ThisFileDirectory = `<root>/tests/windows/win-diagnostics/`. `..` → tests/windows; `..` → tests; `..` → root. Then `windows/OsakaConnect.Windows/...` = `<root>/windows/...`. Correct.\n\nPotential issue: On Linux, backslashes in path property — MSBuild normalizes; EnableWindowsTargeting. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: `Exists('$(ProductProject)')` with a path containing `..` works.\n\nPotential issue: xUnit 2.9.2 + Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 17.11.1 works on net8.0-windows.\n\nPotential issue: `xunit.runner.visualstudio` 2.8.2 supports net8.0. Yes.\n\nPotential concern: `ProductFactAttribute` is `public sealed class` deriving from `FactAttribute`, but no `[AttributeUsage]`; inherited from FactAttribute? AttributeUsage is not inherited on derived? AttributeUsageAttribute has Inherited = true, so fine.\n\nPotential issue: xUnit's test discovery requires the attribute type to be `Xunit.FactAttribute`-assignable — yes.\n\nPotential issue: xUnit analyzer xUnit1000 for the attribute? no.\n\nPotential issue: `Assert.DoesNotContain(\"at \", shown!)` — xUnit v2.9 signature: `public static void DoesNotContain(string expectedSubstring, string? actualString)` maybe. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: Chinese method names — I used English.\n\nPotential issue: In InviteCodeTests, `Assert.True(condition, message)` where message uses interpolation with `{Show(code)}` fine.\n\nPotential issue: `Assert.False(redacted is null, ...)` then `Assert.Equal(item.Out, redacted)` — nullable warning only.\n\nOne more consideration: \"读共享向量文件，按相对仓库根路径定位\" — done via walking up to repo root.\n\n\"被测类型名 ErrorPresenter/LogRedactor/InviteCode.IsValid 来自 brief，命名空间待对齐放顶部\" — done.\n\n\"每个脚本文件开头注释写：用途、前置环境、运行命令、覆盖的 acceptance 编号\" — done for cs files; csproj has用途/前置/运行; README covers. ProductSurface header says 覆盖. SharedVectors header says 覆盖. Good.\n\n\"测试的是用户可见行为（退出码、HTTP 响应、页面标识、显示文案）\" — we assert display text / redacted log output / bool validation. Fine.\n\n\"产品代码未交付时：测试必须清楚输出待测：模块未交付并以 pytest skip（或脚本退出码 0 + 该提示）结束\" — xUnit skip reason. Exit code 0? `dotnet test` with skipped tests returns 0. Yes.\n\n\"不能伪装通过\" — skipped, not passed.\n\nNow: should I add a script to run tests (e.g., run-tests.sh) that prints \"待测：模块未交付\" when windows/ missing and exits 0? The task says \"写最小测试脚本\" and \"脚本顶部标注待 CI\". They might expect a test project only. \"产品代码未交付时...以 pytest skip（或脚本退出码 0 + 该提示）结束\" allows xUnit skip. Fine.\n\nHowever, one issue: `dotnet test` may fail at restore/build if there's no product project? No, our project is standalone. Restore needs NuGet network in CI (normal).\n\nAnother issue: The test project has no product reference today (path absent), so it compiles. ProductFact ctor calls TryResolve → AppDomain assemblies (no product) then Assembly.Load(\"OsakaConnect.Windows\") throws FileNotFoundException → caught → null → Skip. Good.\n\nCould `Assembly.Load` throw something not exception-derived? No.\n\nSecurity: `try { ... } catch (Exception)` acceptable here (test harness). Ponytail says error handling not cut. Fine.\n\nNow, should tests verify the `mask` field from redaction.json? Not needed.\n\nOne subtle problem: A4 vector case `\"Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi\"` → expected `\"Authorization: Bearer ***\"`. The redactor method might be named differently, but constant.\n\nOne subtle problem: for A15 valid case `\" 7X2KQ9MZ \"` with leading/trailing spaces, reflection passes as-is; product trims. Good.\n\nNow let me reconsider the ErrorPresenter method shape. The product may expose `Present(Exception ex)` rather than `Present(string code)`. My test would fail with \"找不到入口 ErrorPresenter.Present/1\"? Actually it finds a method with 1 parameter (Exception) and invokes with a string → `ArgumentException` (Object of type System.String cannot be converted to System.Exception). That's a runtime failure after delivery, signaling misalignment. The comment says align method/entry. But could we make it more robust by matching parameter type to argument? Minimal improvement: in `Call`, match parameter count AND parameter type compatibility:\n\n```csharp\n.FirstOrDefault(m => m.Name == methodName && m.GetParameters().Length == args.Length\n    && m.GetParameters().Zip(args, (p, a) => a is null ? !p.ParameterType.IsValueType : p.ParameterType.IsInstanceOfType(a)).All(ok => ok))\n```\nThis picks the overload taking string. If only Exception exists and we pass string, no match → clear error. That's slightly better. But adds code. For InviteCode bool return, no overload issue. For LogRedactor maybe overloads `Redact(string)` and `Redact(Exception)`; matching types picks string. Worth it? It's 3 lines. Ponytail says correct on edge cases between equal options. I'll add a simple compatibility check.\n\nActually `IsInstanceOfType(null)` returns false, so handle null: `a is null ? !p.ParameterType.IsValueType : p.ParameterType.IsInstanceOfType(a)`. For nullable value types (e.g., string arg won't be null except invite code; parameter string is reference). Fine.\n\nAdd helper:\n```csharp\nprivate static bool Accepts(ParameterInfo[] parameters, object?[] args) =>\n    parameters.Length == args.Length &&\n    parameters.Zip(args).All(pair =>\n        pair.Second is null ? !pair.First.ParameterType.IsValueType : pair.First.ParameterType.IsInstanceOfType(pair.Second));\n```\n`Zip` tuple element names: `.Zip(args)` returns IEnumerable<(TFirst First, TSecond Second)> in .NET 6+. Name them `p.First`/`p.Second`? The tuple names are `First` and `Second`. Use lambda `(p, a) =>` with index-based? Simpler loop:\n\n```csharp\nprivate static bool ShapeMatches(MethodInfo method, object?[] args)\n{\n    var parameters = method.GetParameters();\n    if (parameters.Length != args.Length) return false;\n    for (var i = 0; i < parameters.Length; i++)\n    {\n        var value = args[i];\n        if (value is null)\n        {\n            if (parameters[i].ParameterType.IsValueType) return false;\n        }\n        else if (!parameters[i].ParameterType.IsInstanceOfType(value))\n        {\n            return false;\n        }\n    }\n    return true;\n}\n```\nThen `FirstOrDefault(m => m.Name == methodName && ShapeMatches(m, args))`. Good.\n\nBut note: method may accept `string?` (reference) with null → matches. Good.\n\nAlso methods might be generic; IsInstanceOfType fine.\n\nLet me update ProductSurface.\n\nAnother consideration: `GetMethods` includes inherited object methods; name check filters.\n\nNow, also, what about a method where the string parameter is nullable annotated — runtime type still System.String. Good.\n\nLet me apply the edit.","signature":"1e5a9ac3-d8ce-49ea-9aea-ec343842ed8b"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":369,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":49280,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec7e012c-bf97-4a00-b1a5-b32ee1d3c38b","uuid":"c7c39722-04d9-48ad-b15c-22447b3795e5","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:04:37.018Z","thinking_duration_ms":11598,"thinking_display":"updates"}
